# Durable scope and conversation context for unattended recovery.
exists su name WordNet sweep run id ob text "wordnet-sense-compounds-62e8847575150acbfc937d30" be text ya
exists su name WordNet sweep artifact directory ob text "artifacts/wordnet-sense-compounds-62e8847575150acbfc937d30" be text ya
exists su name WordNet sweep newspaper ob text "newspaper/wordnet-sense-compounds-62e8847575150acbfc937d30.pya" be text ya
exists su name WordNet sweep command ob text "node command/wordnet_sense_compound_refinery.mjs" be text ya
exists su name WordNet sweep check interval minutes ob num 60 be num ya
exists su name WordNet sweep recovery policy ob text "Check the lock owner and durable artifacts. Recent writes or an active provider duty mean the sweep is still working. Spark-X may decide wait, resume, or blocked; deterministic checks must confirm stopped, incomplete, no live lock, and healthy Housekeeper before resume. Resume the same run id under persistent tmux and verify its process owns the sweep lock. Keep accepted ledgers and evidence append-only. Do not let the recovery model edit code or artifacts." be text ya
exists su name WordNet sweep prior incident ob text "The earlier process stopped near 18:31 local time with a stale lock owner pid. No OOM kill was confirmed. Treat OOM as a hypothesis only; inspect current process, artifacts, host memory, and Housekeeper evidence before concluding." be text ya
exists su name WordNet sweep conversation context ob text "This is the broad frequency-ordered Princeton and WordNet synset intersection sweep, including the zero-tag remainder, to attach uncovered synsets to existing Pyash atoms or create useful two-component compounds. The current pipeline limits compounds to two atoms, filters already linked synsets, preserves canonical accepted links, and writes appendable Pyash ledgers plus a newspaper. Earlier work identified cache retention and repeated whole-cache hashing as memory and batch-rollover risks; those were fixed and committed as 23048f5998e8725c9bae23867fdc9db9b2cfec01. The restarted run had 62,466 remaining at the last recorded checkpoint; read current artifacts for the current number." be text ya
exists su name WordNet sweep invariants ob text "Never start a second sweep while the run lock belongs to the live sweep. Never overwrite or delete accepted sense, compound, progress, translation, composition, or newspaper evidence. Unset PYA_MIND_RESPONSE, PYA_HEAR_FIXTURE, PYA_PIPER_FIXTURE, and PYA_GPU_HOUSEKEEPER_FIXTURE for every real run. Route inference through GPU Housekeeper. Preserve unrelated working tree changes. Do not broaden into unrelated vocabulary work." be text ya
exists su name WordNet sweep recovery model ob text "SparkLLM/Spark-X2.6-4B:q4_k_m" be text ya
exists su name WordNet sweep recovery procedure ob text "Read the latest incident and sweep log, confirm the current run id, remaining count, lock owner, and configured Housekeeper status. For a stopped incomplete run with no live lock, resume only through node world/house/refinery-watchdog/program/resume-wordnet-sweep.mjs under a persistent tmux session. That entry point reads this Pyash run id and uses the existing refinery API. Remove PYA_MIND_RESPONSE and every PYA_*_FIXTURE variable. Resolve the Housekeeper from configure/secret.pya before starting; use the Housekeeper queue for every model call. Keep the same run id and append-only artifacts." be text ya
exists su name WordNet sweep post-restart review ob text "On a later hourly check, after the resumed process appends a new completed-batch event, compare the saved pre-restart failure with new durable progress. Include process id, active-process, live-lock-conflict, lock path, remaining count, and latest activity so the review distinguishes a healthy active sweep from an absent lock. Use a separate Spark-X Housekeeper call to record evidence-based root cause, confidence, smallest general fix, and focused regression test plan. Save each attempt's prompt and response separately from the resume decision, with a distinct Housekeeper identity. Retry malformed responses; recover only one missing final outer JSON brace when the rest parses completely. A separate coding turn can implement and test the plan; Spark-X never edits code or sweep artifacts. Preserve the run id and all accepted artifacts." be text ya
exists su name WordNet sweep recovery lesson ob text "A prior invalid Kwon index header followed an incompatible experimental index rebuild. The indexes were rebuilt with the current format and all four lookup kinds passed. For a repeated header failure, inspect the index header and run node command/vocab_lookup_index.mjs to rebuild from canonical catalogs before resuming the same sweep. Never rewrite sweep ledgers to repair a lookup index." be text ya
